{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02267",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 6.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.12,
      "end_seconds": 12.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.24,
      "end_seconds": 18.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "It's sudden confusion over a day, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.3,
      "end_seconds": 23.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.97,
      "end_seconds": 33.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.51,
      "end_seconds": 37.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.83,
      "end_seconds": 73.48,
      "duration_seconds": 34.65,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get not knowing where she is as well. I've had a fever too, for about a week. About fever, honestly, a couple of times a week. The not knowing where she is? That's been for three days. I've also had seeing things that aren't there, for about two weeks. With seeing things that aren't there, maybe a six out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.35,
      "end_seconds": 88.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.11,
      "end_seconds": 93.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Hmm, it's hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 98.74,
      "end_seconds": 104.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.4,
      "end_seconds": 108.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.57,
      "end_seconds": 114.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.61,
      "end_seconds": 117.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Okay, are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.32,
      "end_seconds": 121.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.79,
      "end_seconds": 126.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.04,
      "end_seconds": 133.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.16,
      "end_seconds": 137.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.67,
      "end_seconds": 141.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.62,
      "end_seconds": 145.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.68,
      "end_seconds": 157.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "Yes, I had my appendix taken out, when I was in my twenties. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.34,
      "end_seconds": 166.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.31,
      "end_seconds": 171.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.19,
      "end_seconds": 180.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.13,
      "end_seconds": 183.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.51,
      "end_seconds": 187.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.79,
      "end_seconds": 196.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.68,
      "end_seconds": 204.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure in your file as well. Any sign of fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.12,
      "end_seconds": 209.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Not at all, uh, no fall."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.08,
      "end_seconds": 219.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, head injury or weakness on one side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.11,
      "end_seconds": 227.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "I, I haven't had chest pain, head injury or weakness on one side, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.48,
      "end_seconds": 230.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.59,
      "end_seconds": 235.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "No, you know, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 246.07,
      "end_seconds": 254.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.87,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 19, pressure 108 over 78, temp 38.7 degrees, oxygen saturation is 95 percent, pulse 104."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.92,
      "end_seconds": 257.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.06,
      "end_seconds": 261.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.42,
      "end_seconds": 263.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.28,
      "end_seconds": 285.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "She is drowsy, hot, disoriented, and her blood pressure is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.95,
      "end_seconds": 293.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.85,
      "end_seconds": 326.67,
      "duration_seconds": 23.82,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I don't have a clear answer today: delirium from an infection is possible, and so is dehydration. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had sudden confusion over a day, and no chest pain or weakness on one side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.51,
      "end_seconds": 328.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 330.19,
      "end_seconds": 336.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a urine dipstick before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.61,
      "end_seconds": 364.17,
      "duration_seconds": 25.56,
      "text": "Right, thank you. Let's get a chest X-ray, for fever and confusion. She needs to go to hospital today for fluids and antibiotics. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. I'd like you to see the emergency team as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.1,
      "end_seconds": 374.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.78,
      "end_seconds": 378.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Yes, I'll bear that in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.36,
      "end_seconds": 391.08,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "If it hasn't settled in two weeks, we'd think about blood tests, but not now. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.07,
      "end_seconds": 393.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.55,
      "end_seconds": 402.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "I'd like you back straight away. Right, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.62,
      "end_seconds": 406.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.18,
      "end_seconds": 410.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}